{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others","id":1082756,"title":"Several questions regarding the Syndicate(and others)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-23T13:37:41-07:00","id":1082756,"title":"Several questions regarding the Syndicate(and others)","content":"Currently I'm re-reading revised CB to Technocracy play. And I have discovered a number of intriguing statements related to the Syndicate. Here are some of the most curious.<br /> <br /> Every answer, help, advise, opinion, supposition, speculation and conjecture would be gladly appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Syndicate to Iteration X:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They craft critical components to the world of finance. Iterator engineers provide active security for all the world\u2019s financial institutions \u2014 custodial and investment banks, financial services firms, government treasuries, stock markets, etc. (the so-called \u201cbulge bracket\u201d) \u2014 from Virtual Adept assholes. Of course, the smaller, consumer-level banks and credit unions get looked after too, but they\u2019re not priority targets. Iterators also work with Financiers to pioneer the future of digital banking, one that will instill in the Masses trust rather than fear. Without them, the Syndicate would not be able to forge the next great age of commerce. </div> </div> </div>Does that mean the Syndicate is controlling and directing all the world's financial institution and subcontracting the security work to the Iteration X? Or they are merely arranging those institutions' contract with the Iterators?<br /> <br /> Syndicate to Void Engineers:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They keep submitting requests for weapons and military training in order to counter something they call \u201cThreat Null,\u201d but don\u2019t shed much light on. </div> </div> </div>Why the Void Engineers need weapons and military training from the Syndicate? Both their weapons and training are infinitely more advanced than the Syndicate. It is likely comparing Star Trek Federation military to US &quot;Future Soldiers&quot;. Really, Syndicate has nothing to offer to the VE except Primal Energy.<br /> <br /> Another interesting quote is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> De-prioritizing space exploration in the West has helped to lessen their hold on government and public alike (though, not without resentment) and sends a clear message that they need to cover their bottom line or else. </div> </div> </div>I have no problem to understand Syndicate possesses more than enough political clout to de-prioritize space exploration in the West, even though political and governmental sphere is usually NWO's purview. However, I'm not able to see why the Syndicate moved against and sabotaged VE's efforts.<br /> <br /> Especially if we take account Void Engineers opinion to the Syndicate;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Frankly, that makes the Syndicate easier to work with. They\u2019re trying to sell us a future; it\u2019s not hard to see the Enlightened puppet strings around the birth of commercial space flight. </div> </div> </div>So the Syndicate is de-prioritizing government space exploration while establishing commercial space flight? It is a pure inconsistency...but one could think it is correspond with capitalistic agenda of the Corporate Convention.<br /> <br /> Syndicate to Vampires;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the other hand, some of their longer-lived ilk have entrenched themselves in Consensual economy. Honestly, it\u2019s hard not to respect the power that comes from being able to invest in an institution for decades or even centuries \u2014 though don\u2019t mistake that respect for vampiric reverence overall. </div> </div> </div>So why the Syndicate respects elder vampires? Being able to invest an institution for centuries is nothing exceptional or outstanding by itself, if your have indefinite time.<br /> <br /> Syndicate to other Deviants;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In spite of the Void Engineer\u2019s reports, there are no such things as ghosts, faeries, demons, etc. They serve as entertaining (and profitable) fiction, nothing more. </div> </div> </div>Does that mean the Syndicate is completely ignorant about existence of such entities? Or they simply do not acknowledge these as mythical, arcane beings? After all, VE use terms such as PLE or extradimensional creatures. And even if the Syndics are woefully unversed in DS, they can see and interact with ghosts, spirits(well, if they choose to take a form and wreck havoc), faeries and demons - and in case of ghosts, they are fully capable of sensing and sterilizing Haunts with Primal Energy.<br /> <br /> Disbursements and Primal Venture:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disbursements also contains the largest and most secure Ventures under Technocratic control, packaging and distributing the very essence of reality to aid our efforts and projects across the world. </div> </div> </div>Does it mean Disbursements directly manage and control certain international corporations and global conglomerates and extract Primal Energy from the operations?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Syndicate controls the largest collection of Nodes and Ventures of any Enlightened organization in the world, and they are maintained almost exclusively by the Extraction Division. These specialists not only arrange for the security and secrecy of node locations, but also harvest, distill, and distribute the resulting condensed Primal Energy to operatives within and without the Convention. </div> </div> </div>Do it means 1) Syndicate separate natural nodes and industrial Ventures. 2) Syndicate has trained experts of node extraction. 3) Aforementioned 'the largest and most secure Ventures' are under direct control of Extraction Division. 4) Syndicate provides secrecy and military security of not only Enlightened Prime Ventures, but also Primal Node locations. 5) Syndicate paradigm of Venture is compatible with Nodes...or node extraction specialists have different paradigm of Prime from other, 'normal' Syndicate members. 6) Technocratic Unions generate several orders of magnitude greater Primal Energy than any other supernatural/paranormal(&quot;Enlightened&quot; - or this usage is solely limited to the Technocratic Conventions?) organization in the world, but it is still not sufficient to fund various Technocratic projects and endeavors?<br /> <br /> Media Control and Newspaper:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When Media Control was in its infancy, the original amalgams attempted to assume control of what was then the cutting edge of journalism:<br /> newspapers. They met with stiff competition in the form of the news conglomerates of the day, especially William Randolph Hearst, who along with his colleagues rebuffed any offer of a merger. </div> </div> </div>So William Randolph Hearst and his ilk was a non-aligned cabal of Mind mages? If not, how they were able to resist against powerful Ars Cupiditae and Mind Procedures routinely utilized by the Media Control?<br /> <br /> <br /> And finally, why the Syndicate is so deeply involved in organized crime and illegal drug trades? Given the Syndicate's scope of operations and revenue it generates, it is redundant at best, degenerative at worst. If profit is mattered, they can reap even greater profit via investing international corporations, global financial institutions, Primal Ventures, etc. Is it merely another means of Mass control?<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, Progenitors CB makes me wonder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We had the best of intentions. The need for the release and glamor these street drugs provide is an incurable part of human existence. Curbing demand was dismissed as impossible, so the only recourse was to make them safer, cleaner, and with minimal side effects. That was until the Syndicate got their grubby mitts in the business. They have changed the street labs into the biggest source of income for not just the Progenitors, but <i>the Union as a whole</i>. Long-gone are the days of concern over the purity and safety of the product. The street lab organizations take their cues from their Syndicate masters, who allow the Progenitors in the field only enough authority to insure smooth daily operations. The strategic direction is solely focused on profit, and has been for decades now. </div> </div> </div>I can readily dismiss it as a gross overstatement or anti-Syndicate propaganda. But still, the statement itself is confounding as hell. How on earth drug trade is more profitable than controlling global finance and industries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-23-2017, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T22:12:00-07:00","id":1082903,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I have to be honest. A lot of this was difficult to muddle through and might have been parsed in a more concise manner. I apologize for my own failures to read it in the manner it oughta be.<br /> <br /> The bit about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Syndicate to Void Engineers: <br /> They keep submitting requests for weapons and military training in order to counter something they call \u201cThreat Null,\u201d but don\u2019t shed much light on.<br /> <br /> <br /> Why the Void Engineers need weapons and military training from the Syndicate? Both their weapons and training are infinitely more advanced than the Syndicate. It is likely comparing Star Trek Federation military to US &quot;Future Soldiers&quot;. Really, Syndicate has nothing to offer to the VE except Primal Energy. </div> </div> </div>Well, we see in CB Rev: Void Engineers that everything they build costs a lot. The Void Ships, for example, run in the billions. The $yndicate is the branch of the Union that has that money, and the VEs have to play nice with them/convince them to spend all that cash on them in order to continue building Voidships to fight Threat Null (all without telling the $yndicate and the rest of the Union about Threat Null). It's not just primal energy that they have, it's resources that other people find valuable enough to exchange for goods and services. <br /> <br /> Further, The Syndicate may not have the same kind of military-type operators, but how do you think the VEs can recruit theirs? 'Travel the Void in our Ethership. Meet our Borg-Lookalikes. Get assimilated by them!' Doesn't fill me with the same zeal as 'Oh, I get six figures *and* I get to zip around space in a Daedalus-class? sign me up!' If that makes sense?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry it's just one section, but it's a little jammed for me. I'll look at the rest later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T08:48:12-07:00","id":1083031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arzie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1082903#post1082903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I have to be honest. A lot of this was difficult to muddle through and might have been parsed in a more concise manner. I apologize for my own failures to read it in the manner it oughta be.<br /> <br /> The bit about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, we see in CB Rev: Void Engineers that everything they build costs a lot. The Void Ships, for example, run in the billions. The $yndicate is the branch of the Union that has that money, and the VEs have to play nice with them/convince them to spend all that cash on them in order to continue building Voidships to fight Threat Null (all without telling the $yndicate and the rest of the Union about Threat Null). It's not just primal energy that they have, it's resources that other people find valuable enough to exchange for goods and services.<br /> <br /> Further, The Syndicate may not have the same kind of military-type operators, but how do you think the VEs can recruit theirs? 'Travel the Void in our Ethership. Meet our Borg-Lookalikes. Get assimilated by them!' Doesn't fill me with the same zeal as 'Oh, I get six figures *and* I get to zip around space in a Daedalus-class? sign me up!' If that makes sense?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry it's just one section, but it's a little jammed for me. I'll look at the rest later.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to feel sorry at all. I appreciate your opinion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:15:54-07:00","id":1083149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Syndicate to Iteration X:<br /> <br /> Does that mean the Syndicate is controlling and directing all the world's financial institution and subcontracting the security work to the Iteration X? Or they are merely arranging those institutions' contract with the Iterators?</div> </div> </div> </div>Syndicate supposedly controls global finance and financial institutions of all the world. So yes, Syndicate directly owns such institutions. And they have to own them - if not, how they can arrange contract with engineering companies controlled by Iteration X? I have never heard banks and other financial institutions single out their own exclusive security based on outside advisers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Syndicate to other Deviants;<br /> <br /> Does that mean the Syndicate is completely ignorant about existence of such entities? Or they simply do not acknowledge these as mythical, arcane beings? After all, VE use terms such as PLE or extradimensional creatures. And even if the Syndics are woefully unversed in DS, they can see and interact with ghosts, spirits(well, if they choose to take a form and wreck havoc), faeries and demons - and in case of ghosts, they are fully capable of sensing and sterilizing Haunts with Primal Energy.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It seems Syndicate knows existence of such entities but does not acknowledge their mystical connotations. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the Void Engineers need weapons and military training from the Syndicate? Both their weapons and training are infinitely more advanced than the Syndicate. It is likely comparing Star Trek Federation military to US &quot;Future Soldiers&quot;. Really, Syndicate has nothing to offer to the VE except Primal Energy.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fresh meats to grinder, I suppose. After all, Void Engineers do not have enough cadets and marines to sustain constant severe losses inflicted on by the dread Threat Null. Someone has to provide backbone...or meat shields to absorb, or at lest mitigate, losses. Remember the Syndicate holds near monopoly on private security and military consultancies, mercenary companies and other diverse paramilitaries. They are also exerting tremendous influence on defense industries. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it mean Disbursements directly manage and control certain international corporations and global conglomerates and extract Primal Energy from the operations?<br /> <br /> Do it means 1) Syndicate separate natural nodes and industrial Ventures. 2) Syndicate has trained experts of node extraction. 3) Aforementioned 'the largest and most secure Ventures' are under direct control of Extraction Division. 4) Syndicate provides secrecy and military security of not only Enlightened Prime Ventures, but also Primal Node locations. 5) Syndicate paradigm of Venture is compatible with Nodes...or node extraction specialists have different paradigm of Prime from other, 'normal' Syndicate members. 6) Technocratic Unions generate several orders of magnitude greater Primal Energy than any other supernatural/paranormal(&quot;Enlightened&quot; - or this usage is solely limited to the Technocratic Conventions?) organization in the world, but it is still not sufficient to fund various Technocratic projects and endeavors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Node extraction specialists may indeed have somewhat different paradigm of Prime to their workmates. And Technocratic operations are extremely resource intensive. I think NWO and Syndicate probably spend as much Primal Energy and other multitudes of resources as R&amp;D Conventions, if not more...even though providing accurate, elaborate examples is outside of my capacity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Media Control and Newspaper:<br /> <br /> So William Randolph Hearst and his ilk was a non-aligned cabal of Mind mages? If not, how they were able to resist against powerful Ars Cupiditae and Mind Procedures routinely utilized by the Media Control?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They are most likely independent willworkers. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can readily dismiss it as a gross overstatement or anti-Syndicate propaganda. But still, the statement itself is confounding as hell. How on earth drug trade is more profitable than controlling global finance and industries?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Definitely gross hyperbole. Enforcers operations provide only a fraction of Syndicate profits. Most of Syndicate revenues are coming from D</span></span></span>isbursements and Financiers. Enforcers are a fringe, relatively minor Methodology.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sadly, these sections are all I am able to deliberate answer. Sorry. I hope to Ajax or Five Eyes notice this post. Since I'm equally curious about the various </span></span></span>queries <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">you have offered. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 04-24-2017, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T13:22:20-07:00","id":1083153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1083149#post1083149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They are most likely independent willworkers. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Or Extraordinary Citizens with Fascination.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Hosting <a href=\"http://opx-finalfrontier.wikidot.com\" target=\"_blank\">Outpost Phoenix</a>, an Non-Affiliated, Live-Action Star Trek <a href=\"https://discord.gg/6zwnyzm\" target=\"_blank\">Discord</a> Sim. New players are always welcome!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11235-arzie","name":"Arzie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T22:14:34-07:00","id":1083339,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll do what I can.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Syndicate to Iteration X:<br /> Does that mean the Syndicate is controlling and directing all the world's financial institution and subcontracting the security work to the Iteration X? Or they are merely arranging those institutions' contract with the Iterators?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think we have to arrive there - if anything, the Syndicate disavows such direct control (The Financiers blurb in RevSynd says specifically that they're hands-off, etc.). A few points:<br /> <br /> <b>1.)</b> Remember that - through outfits such as Plexic - the Syndicate is placing Iterator technology into the hands of Sleeper industries and customers. The nanosecond high-frequency trading algorithms that form such a large block of economic activity, for instance, were born from Iterator (and Difference Engineer) efforts. The high-tech infrastructure of the cutting edge of the financial market is proprietary hypertech - a black box containing all sorts of backdoors and protective routines that the client is never aware of.<br /> <br /> <b>2.) </b>The Iterators also have agents and AIs operating in the Digitial Web, the &quot;internet astral plane&quot;, shielding sensitive computer systems from cross-dimensional tampering. These resources won't be on <i>every </i>financial system, but if you tried to cause Knight Capital Group to implode you'd probably run into guards.<br /> <br /> Of course, Knight could implode on its own due to operator error, because reality is unrealistic.<br /> <br /> <b>3.)</b> If an Iterator hacker was monitoring and defending a Sleeper financial institution's systems 24/7, even without permission, how would they know? It's not like they have to ask.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Syndicate to Void Engineers:<br /> Why the Void Engineers need weapons and military training from the Syndicate? Both their weapons and training are infinitely more advanced than the Syndicate. It is likely comparing Star Trek Federation military to US &quot;Future Soldiers&quot;. Really, Syndicate has nothing to offer to the VE except Primal Energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The controlling metaphor of Revised Syndicate (right or wrong) is that the Syndicates hold the purse strings of the Union - both in terms of money and in terms of Prime.<br /> <br /> The Void Engineers ask the Syndicate for weapons and soldiers in the same way that the Army asks Congress for weapons and soldiers - they mean the Engineers have to make a case to the Syndicate for why they <i>need</i> a new explododeathcannon and funding to run a training program to produce a hundred new redshirts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Syndicate is de-prioritizing government space exploration while establishing commercial space flight? It is a pure inconsistency...but one could think it is correspond with capitalistic agenda of the Corporate Convention.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate has decided that their spoiled teenager needs a lesson in responsibility, so they're making Voido pay rent and get a part-time job.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate describes undercutting the hold on government and the public consciousness as an attempt to make the voidies recognize that <i>things cost money. </i>To return to our purse strings metaphor, the VEs are (as far as the Syndicate is concerned) an expensive government program that's got so much popularity and inertia that they've stopped making efficient and responsible use of the taxpayer's dollar. By cutting off the gravy train and pushing space exploration into a private, profit-driven model, the Syndicate is giving the voidies a dose of reality.<br /> <br /> (I think it's interesting that the thing I find jarringly inconsistent in the Syndicate &quot;other Conventions&quot; section is different than what other people get hung up on.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Syndicate to Vampires:<br /> So why the Syndicate respects elder vampires? Being able to invest an institution for centuries is nothing exceptional or outstanding by itself, if your have indefinite time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd read that as: They respect the <i>power </i>and <i>depth - </i>the financial resources the vampires have under their thumbs, and in their commitment to shepherding their holdings. Kindred aren't just immortal, they're territorial - and, when it comes to their territory, surprisingly cunning. (And we probably shouldn't think of Kindred as casually immortal - Kindred society is cutthroat in ways that make the corporate shark tank look like a hug box.) Even a slick Syndicate operator can respect the kind of ruthlessness and agility it takes for a vampire elder to hold onto their assets in the face of dozens of competitors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Syndicate to other Deviants;<br /> Does that mean the Syndicate is completely ignorant about existence of such entities? Or they simply do not acknowledge these as mythical, arcane beings? After all, VE use terms such as PLE or extradimensional creatures. And even if the Syndics are woefully unversed in DS, they can see and interact with ghosts, spirits(well, if they choose to take a form and wreck havoc), faeries and demons - and in case of ghosts, they are fully capable of sensing and sterilizing Haunts with Primal Energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've fielded this one <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/987239-syndicate-and-various-supernaturals?p=990103#post990103\">before</a>, actually. I don't think a Syndicate Enforcer that encountered a manifest spirit, Risen, or fomor would associate what they fought with any Voidie prank. It's an alien, or a mutant, or some Marauder freak. The Syndicate probably also follows the Union/Void trend in not ascribing particular value, meaning, or &quot;personhood&quot; to these entities. A ghost, if it exists, isn't a person. It's a strange psychic phenomenon, and it can't teach you anything useful. Flip the house and move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disbursements and Primal Venture:<br /> Does it mean Disbursements directly manage and control certain international corporations and global conglomerates and extract Primal Energy from the operations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Direct management wouldn't agree with the rest of the Convention Book, so I suspect that Disbursements is responsible for keeping tabs on, nourishing, and protecting both valuable Nodes and important Ventures. Some of these Ventures will include hypertech businesses that the Syndicate owns directly, so Disbursements may be the owner-of-record for AEZIR and etc., but that's an outlier.<br /> <br /> Disbursements owns and operates the geothermal harvester the Syndicate builds on top of a caern*, and has agents in place to make sure that nobody meddles with the board of an important Venture. Their operatives also extract Prime from these sources - both to pay the bills and to make sure that nobody else does it. That last step's important, because any young turk Enforcer with more Primal Utility than sense can cause a management disaster in a valuable Venture by drawing more Prime than it can spare. Disbursements are the Very Serious People that make sure that nobody goes cowboy with the Union's quintessential resources and everybody gets paid on time.<br /> <br /> *The notion of the Syndicate tapping nodes predates the Primal Utility model, so the Union probably does have some &quot;Prime&quot; sources and some &quot;Primal Utility&quot; sources. Offhand I'd say that in the Revised era you should assume they have to use a conjunctional effect to tap into them - such as Forces/Primal Utility to tap a volcanic caern.<br /> <br /> On your 6.) I'd take the &quot;largest collection&quot; to mean that the Syndicate, as a whole, has its claws in more Nodes and Ventures than any other Convention, Craft, or Tradition - the other &quot;Awakened/Enlightened&quot; players. It may also, by the numbers, hold more quint reserves than, say, the Garou Nation, if only because caerns are fading, but nothing in that statement requires it - the scope is limited. I see no reason to think that the Syndicate is in an &quot;orders of magnitude&quot; situation, though - they could have 101% the value of the next best competitor and the statement would still be true. I assume they hold <i>more </i>than anyone else, by some margin, but even <i>more</i> is insufficient to cover everything the Union's operations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Media Control and Newspaper:<br /> So William Randolph Hearst and his ilk was a non-aligned cabal of Mind mages? If not, how they were able to resist against powerful Ars Cupiditae and Mind Procedures routinely utilized by the Media Control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Use magic to <i>seize control </i>of <i>independent, profitable businesses? </i>That's Pinko Craftmason talk, <i>comrade.</i> But really, Sleepers occasionally pull one over on the Union, especially when Media Control was in its infancy when Hearst was ascendant - and that sidebar is at least somewhat a cute little aside about the death of print media.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, why the Syndicate is so deeply involved in organized crime and illegal drug trades? Given the Syndicate's scope of operations and revenue it generates, it is redundant at best, degenerative at worst. If profit is mattered, they can reap even greater profit via investing international corporations, global financial institutions, Primal Ventures, etc. Is it merely another means of Mass control?</div> </div> </div> </div>Organized crime and the drug trade <i>are </i>international business. They <i>are </i>Primal Ventures. They represent vibrant, profitable markets that Sleepers <i>want, </i>want badly enough to flaunt the law. If the Syndicate didn't sit on these markets, someone else would, and an agile street gang that peddles meth may well produce <b><i>more </i></b>Primal energy - more <i>real value - </i>than a moribund and hidebound industry that moves millions of dollars a quarter. The Syndicate, in their infinite benevolence, does not discriminate against valid and energetic markets just because of shortsighted government regulation. It also serves as an excellent way to lay hands on illegal and quasi-legal influence, and to make sure that these gray and black market operations don't get <i>too </i>dangerous to the Masses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others#post1082756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can readily dismiss it as a gross overstatement or anti-Syndicate propaganda. But still, the statement itself is confounding as hell. How on earth drug trade is more profitable than controlling global finance and industries?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gross overstatement.<br /> <br /> Although it would not be impossible for the cash value <i>extracted </i>from the drug trade to be a larger number than that <i>extracted </i>from managing and advising the financial sector - just because the Syndicate has a guy that assists management for a company worth a billion dollars, it doesn't mean the Syndicate just made a billion dollars. The Progenitor drugs are one of the few products that the Union <i>directly </i>produces and sells.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;more profitable than controlling global finance and industries&quot; puts the cart before the horse - <i>does </i>the Syndicate <i>control</i> global finance and international industry?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T01:47:46-07:00","id":1083384,"title":"","content":"You are always most helpful, Thank you for being a kind, enlightened Daimon, Five Eyes. I have some questions, too;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A: Both the Disbursements and Financier operates in economic and corporate sectors and generates net profits for the Union, Prime and otherwise, aren't they? I know their assigned matrix of responsibility and obligation is distinct from each other - Disbursements are bureaucrats and managers and Financiers are counselors and economists first and foremost. Having said that, nonetheless, isn't Disbursements and Financiers suffering significant overlap both in their operational fields, spheres of jurisdiction and role and mandate as the Methodology?<br /> B: So in your vision, the Syndicate's proportional hold of Prime sources is greater than any other Awakened players, including the Garou Nation, but differential margin is not significant?<br /> C: Would you mind if I ask you to cite some examples of NWO and Syndicate's Primal Energy sinks comparable to other Conventions?<br /> D: So do you think Progenitor drugs really could have the highest percentage of the Union's income?<br /> E: I found this intriguing paragraph: &quot;As one of the world\u2019s leading arms patent holders, AEZIR Gmbh keeps hypertech systems in its vaults to awe military and police buyers, but says these prototypes aren\u2019t quite ready for the market.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does it indicate <i>every</i> leading patent holder(arms or otherwise) across the world is in fact Technocratic front and keeps hypertech systems in its vaults?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 04-25-2017, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T07:44:25-07:00","id":1083452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1083384#post1083384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are always most helpful, Thank you for being a kind, enlightened Daimon, Five Eyes. I have some questions, too;<br /> <br /> A: Both the Disbursements and Financier operates in economic and corporate sectors and generates net profits for the Union, Prime and otherwise, aren't they? I know their assigned matrix of responsibility and obligation is distinct from each other - Disbursements are bureaucrats and managers and Financiers are counselors and economists first and foremost. Having said that, nonetheless, isn't Disbursements and Financiers suffering significant overlap both in their operational fields, spheres of jurisdiction and role and mandate as the Methodology?<br /> B: So in your vision, the Syndicate's proportional hold of Prime sources is greater than any other Awakened players, including the Garou Nation, but differential margin is not significant?<br /> C: Would you mind if I ask you to cite some examples of NWO and Syndicate's Primal Energy sinks comparable to other Conventions?<br /> D: So do you think Progenitor drugs really could have the highest percentage of the Union's income?<br /> E: I found this intriguing paragraph: &quot;As one of the world\u2019s leading arms patent holders, AEZIR Gmbh keeps hypertech systems in its vaults to awe military and police buyers, but says these prototypes aren\u2019t quite ready for the market.&quot;<br /> <br /> Does it indicate <i>every</i> leading patent holder(arms or otherwise) across the world is in fact Technocratic front and keeps hypertech systems in its vaults?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> A. Yes, they do overlap. It's worth to remember that they were one single group in the age of the High Guild. They were the powerful Sun Guild, the one in charge of all wealth.<br /> <br /> The problem it's that, as the major responsible of profit, they were becoming too powerful (almost a representation of the whole Convention)...so the high ups of the Union decided to separate the guild in to sub-groups. Financier would deal with controling the world's economy, and Disbursements would have control of the purse string of the Union itself. As I understand it, this means that Financiers get the resources but Disbursements decides how to distribute them in the union. Financiers probably control more money/Prime, but Disbursements it's more powerful within their peers because you will need to answer to them if you want the Quint. This may cause some colision of interests, but it's as intended, to ensure no one becomes powerful enough to control all the resources of the Union. <br /> <br /> B. In MY vision, yes they are. Powerful Caerns/Nodes are powerful, but they are few and far between. Powerful Primal Ventures also are rare, but only the Syndicate can harvest them (only a few mages outside the Convention has PU). Between Nodes and PU they more than likely have the lions share of Quintessence. <br /> <br /> C. What do you mean with Primal Energy sinks?. You mean in what they spend the Quint?. I don't think that the Syndicate as a whole spends as much juice as, say, the ItX with their Artifact factories that are constantly building artificats (that cost a lot of juice each) or the VE and their costly starships and weapons. They &quot;do&quot; produce artifacts, though (those elegant powersuits don't enchant themselves) and may spend a lot of juice trying to prevent Market Correction when they make a big shift in the market (a big ritual, don't want to botch that one, but if it happens you want to have a Prime buffer). Similarly, the NWO may spend Quint in big procedures to clean minds in large areas, to control the internet, and in their radars and Q division devices. <br /> <br /> D. I don't, I think it's an overstatement. But they may be the largest percentage of income that the <i>Progenitors </i>produce for the Union. Syndicate likes the Conventions to produce income, and the Prgenitors can do so via private medical institutions (that some don't want to make because they fell that making medicine private reduces the amount of people that can beneffit from it, which it's true)...and producing drugs, both legal and illegal.<br /> <br /> E. I don't think so. I interpret that to mean that those Technocratic fronts that are &quot;leading patent holder(arms or otherwise)&quot; are allowed to have hypertech systems in their vaults to show them in a controled environment to selected people, in order to prepare the sleepers to accept the new technology that the Union want's to disclose in the near future. <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:03:57-07:00","id":1083553,"title":"","content":"At this rate I'm going to have to run a Syndicate game. There's not a lot of international finance going on in my Dark Ages game, for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1083384#post1083384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A: Both the Disbursements and Financier operates in economic and corporate sectors and generates net profits for the Union, Prime and otherwise, aren't they? I know their assigned matrix of responsibility and obligation is distinct from each other - Disbursements are bureaucrats and managers and Financiers are counselors and economists first and foremost. Having said that, nonetheless, isn't Disbursements and Financiers suffering significant overlap both in their operational fields, spheres of jurisdiction and role and mandate as the Methodology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Look at Disbursement's methodologies again:<br /> 1.) Review and assign the allocation of Union resources to Union projects.<br /> 2.) Correct and sanction mismanagement of Union resources by Union operations.<br /> 3.) Manage and catalog the flow of Union resources into Syndicate coffers and out of those coffers into Syndic hands.<br /> 4.) Manage and defend Union Quintessential holdings, grow their value where possible, and extract their Prime from them for use in Union projects.<br /> <br /> Disbursement only touches the &quot;Sleeper&quot; economy very lightly.<br /> It doesn't make any money - it manages, nurtures, and disburses the money that the Financiers and Enforcers make.<br /> It doesn't create any new business Ventures - it manages and defends those that the other Methodologies have scouted.<br /> <br /> Disbursements can't really &quot;generate profit&quot; - any more than the IRS &quot;generates profit&quot; or the congressional budget &quot;generates profit.&quot; They can manage the Union's money skillfully to grow the stake, or use shrewd accounting to cut back on loss, but that's not the same thing. (When Disbursements <i>is </i>mentioned as making money, it's when Extraction <i>embezzles quint </i>and sells it to line their own pockets.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1083384#post1083384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B: So in your vision, the Syndicate's proportional hold of Prime sources is greater than any other Awakened players, including the Garou Nation, but differential margin is not significant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Significant but not &quot;orders of magnitude.&quot; The Syndicate holds more Prime reserves than any other magely player (and probably numerous non-mage players), but not so much more that Disbursements can be cavalier about how they spend it. It's key to the Syndicate's character that they have to make hard decisions about what to do with limited resources - and it'd be tough to portray their resources as limited if they had ten times as much as anyone else (unless you are imagining that the Union is ten or more times bigger than any other player, which I do not.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1083384#post1083384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">C: Would you mind if I ask you to cite some examples of NWO and Syndicate's Primal Energy sinks comparable to other Conventions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sinks as in expenses? Patching Market Correction, restoring spent Resources, temporal and long-term enchantment of Union assets such as employees and devices. Horizon constructs require a constant tap of earthbound Quint resources, too, so every secret extradimensional prison or training camp is a drain on terrestrial resources. Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1083384#post1083384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">D: So do you think Progenitor drugs really could have the highest percentage of the Union's income?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly - and certainly not income. I think it's a gross overstatement.<br /> <br /> What I meant is more that I think the assumption that the Syndicate rakes in billions or trillions of dollars from financial markets shouldn't be taken as an axiom.<br /> <br /> The Financiers could very well be revenue-neutral and still operate as described - they move around tons of money, but a lot of (perhaps the vast majority of) that money doesn't come out of or go into the Union's pocket, it emerges and returns to the Sleeper economy, doing the Convention's actual job. Individual Financiers have multimillion dollar salaries, but that's an expense, it's a necessary step for Disbursements to keep those agents loyal and make sure they don't take their talents somewhere else. The drug trade having the highest degree of <b>profit </b>might actually be possible, if you imagine that most of what the Syndicate is doing (after paying for everything, including, let's not forget, competitive salaries for Syndics) has a narrow profit margin given the expenses incurred.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Financiers <i>are </i>revenue-neutral, but I think it's important to back up a step. How much money do you think the Syndicate reaps from keeping an eye on the global economy? Do they <i>make </i>that money or simply<i>monitor </i>it? By way of analogy: Is the size of a government's budget particularly relevant to how much money the NWO makes?<br /> <br /> The seed of contention in this thread and several other questions that have cropped up recently starts with the premise that the Syndicate owns - not manages, not advises, not monitors, <i>owns - </i>huge swaths of the global economy. Then, with this assumption in place, other things seem to not make sense, but we should at least be suspicious of the premise first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1083384#post1083384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">E: I found this intriguing paragraph: &quot;As one of the world\u2019s leading arms patent holders, AEZIR Gmbh keeps hypertech systems in its vaults to awe military and police buyers, but says these prototypes aren\u2019t quite ready for the market.&quot; Does it indicate <i>every</i> leading patent holder(arms or otherwise) across the world is in fact Technocratic front and keeps hypertech systems in its vaults?</div> </div> </div> </div>No reason to think that. I suspect that a lot of the super-high-end boutiques for technical industries are fronts, but others are independent, Traditionalist, other-weirdos, Sleepers, etc. Like with the finance industry, the Syndics do the best they can, but they're not perfect, and a lot of trouble seeps through the cracks.<br /> <br /> We do know that the Syndicate tries to ensure that it holds or contests patents on burgeoning hypertech industries that it wants to bring to market or to make sure things that the Union didn't expect <i>don't </i>make it to market (The example amalgam is one such litigator.) So even if the Union doesn't hold the patent to RapiLux's hypertech search algorithm, they can tie it up in court for long enough to hopefully smother it or co-opt the company before they cause any trouble.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:01:06-07:00","id":1083598,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In fact, I had run an all-Syndicate game previously.<br /> <br /> A. Regardless of the Methodology's portfolio, Disbursement agents have their own profession and generate lots of profit. If I remember correctly, The Fallen Tower, Progenitor CB, and other various sourcebooks featured Syndic reps describe Disbursement agents have their sources of income that make lots of money. If they are bureaucratic drones who posses little to no monetary flair, it is very doubtful Syndicate ever recruits them in the first place. NWO bureaucrats can do exactly same jobs if they get the right knowledge and PU paradigm, possibly even better.<br /> <br /> B. I concur. Although I suspect even if the Syndicate generates ten times more quint than OoH, it will still be found wanting to fund all projects conducted by the Union.<br /> <br /> C. Yes, in expenses. Since Union's contact to Horizon and other extradimensional Realm is completely severed in the wake of DA, I think modern Syndicate will be able to divert significant portion of PE to various territorial projects. Besides, could you provide some NWO examples? Also, is it possible Syndicate investing quint in their own research, development and projects? And what 'temporal and long-term enchantment of Union assets' is indicating? Do you mean Prime-invested improvements such as Asset Exploitation?<br /> <br /> D. I concede. Haven't you said vast majority of Union's profit is derived from careful, Enlightened investment?<br /> <br /> E. Agree. Independent, Traditionalist, Nephandi and <i>other</i>-sponsored hypertech firms should be exist.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 04-25-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T13:27:35-07:00","id":1083643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A. Regardless of the Methodology's portfolio, Disbursement agents have their own profession and generate lots of profit. If I remember correctly, The Fallen Tower, Progenitor CB, and other various sourcebooks featured Syndic reps describe Disbursement agents have their sources of income that make lots of money. If they are bureaucratic drones who posses little to no monetary flair, it is very doubtful Syndicate ever recruits them in the first place. NWO bureaucrats can do exactly same jobs if they get the right knowledge and PU paradigm, possibly even better. </div> </div> </div>Sure, a Syndic can have his own money, they're encouraged to have it, and sometimes they own profitable corporations for fun, but this doesn't mean that their purposse it's to control the financial institutions of the world (that's Financers portfolio).<br /> <br /> You incorrectly believe that the job of bureaucraticaly administrating the resources of the Union as something a drone can do. I would say it's the opposite.<br /> <br /> Disbursement are the ones that control all of the activities that the Union, including going to Amalgams and deciding which projects are proffitable or should be funded for other reasons, and which aren't. In order to do this agents need to have knowledge of Hyperscience, they can't be just bean counters, because they have to understand what transpires in the Amalgam. Also they need the financial understanding to know how much they need and guess how much they can earn back, and have enough social intelligence to not get killed by angry mages when you decide not to fund them. Also, this gives Disbursement more power within the Union than any other camp, aka, you don't want NWO take that job, because then the Syndicate it's going to loose the control of which projects get funded, and with that all the power they have within the Union (the Union it's going to become a Balck Box where money enters and the Syndicate isn't going to know what happens with it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-25-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:39:53-07:00","id":1083698,"title":"","content":"Follow-up stuff.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>A:</b> I'm not sure we're talking about the same thing.<br /> <br /> Disbursements includes some of the savviest number-crunchers in the universe, no doubt - but by the time they're handling the money, it's the Union's money. They'll do some light investment with it, sure, but by the time it's in Disbursement's hands, it's money that the Union already has plans to spend, and they can't play around with it. Instead of using Entropy to broadcast which markets they ought to invest in, Disbursements has the much more strenuous task of using Entropy to broadcast which Conventions will need more funding in the next year, which constructs aren't pulling their weight, and where a likely unexpected black swan event will crop up. Plus, they have to have the chops to find all the embezzlement that their mage colleagues are using Enlightened economics to cover up.<br /> <br /> Everyone mocked Dave Proctor from Disbursements when he approved funding for a network of diamond-plated solar reflection satellites back in 1989, but when Ravnos showed up, Dave was a hero. Media Control made a Bond movie in his honor, even.<br /> <br /> Disbursements <i>agents </i>are swimming in cash, of course. For Methodology projects they have access to a deep administrative budget - if Disbursements can spend millions to prevent the misuse of tens of millions, it's a win for everyone. And, on a personal level, they're paid for their work, and they have to be paid handsomely enough that they don't slip a hand into the till - and they know exactly how much the Union can afford to pay, so there's no chance of giving them less and pleading poverty. Disbursements guys are probably richer than their Syndicate peers, on average. (I also wager that Disbursements has a bounty system in place for waste and inefficiency - if you correct the Union's budget, you get a percentage of the savings)<br /> <br /> Making 5% growth with a portfolio worth a million dollars takes a lot of financial savvy, but so does balancing the budget of a multi-billion-dollar governmental organization for the next year.<br /> <br /> <b>C:</b> The shockwaves that shattered the Horizon realms probably also did a number on their geomantic infrastructure, so the nodes in the network may be lost or in need of repair.<br /> <br /> In terms of NWO use, all of those wizbang gadgets and enhanced mirrorshades take Prime to build and charge. While it's not modeled well by the rules, long-term or broad-range Procedures also require a Primal flow to stay operational, so very major acts of information manipulation or social control are probably a chunk of the budget.<br /> <br /> They Syndicate may need some of the Union's Prime to build the extraordinary devices that agents requisition or which are made by Syndicate fronts - it depends on whether you think they make those in-house or if Disbursements (through Procurement) takes them in from other Conventions, but the Syndicate has to budget for it either way. They may also funnel some Prime into their own projects (The Eris front is all-Syndicate, IIRC, so anything they make) but I suspect there's an organizational bias against it - why infuse Prime into a smarthphone, where it'll sit forever doing nothing, when you could funnel that power back into the economy and help build a Venture that pays Prime dividends.<br /> <br /> &quot;Temporal and long-term enhancements&quot; is Prime 2 and Prime 3 enchantment (and to a lesser extent Prime 3/4 creation of Devices/living Devices), yeah.<br /> <br /> <b>D:</b> That would be my estimation - that the majority of the operational funding (and Venture creation) in the Syndicate is coming from the Financiers, who can skim a percent off from all of the money that they handle (as a &quot;consulting fee&quot; if nothing else) and invest it in promising industries - both furthering the Union's goals by growing the sectors the Union wants grown, and turning a profit. Those investments, down the line, empower and grow innovative and enterprising new businesses, which give rise to Primal Ventures. Once funds and ventures have matured, Disbursements takes stewardship of them for long-term maintenance and growth and to make sure they stay viable and safe.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:17:23-07:00","id":1084047,"title":"","content":"Wow. You are all awesome. Thank you guys. Thank you very much.<br /> <br /> Just two more questions. Why the Syndicate is collaborating with some elder vampires and occasional Traditionalists without any hesitation or compunction for the sake of so-called &quot;business&quot;? It can be seen as treason from other elements in the Union. Have they no principles or moral compass as members of the Union? What could the Syndicate gain from it? They are toxic partners at the best of times. Is it worth to take risks? And in any case, what business needs Deviant's assistance to flourish? Is Syndicate too incompetent to stand on its own two feet? <br /> <br /> IIRC, Disbursement agents have their own occupations and manages their own enterprises, as Posthumanity already pointed out. Then where does operatives' profits go? Who gets them? Agents themselves? Disbursements? Union's annual budget? For instance, if a Disbursement agent runs a food chain, it will yield tones of money and PE. Indeed, IIRC, a Disbursement agent was alluded to own a coffee house chain. Someone have to come and collect it. Or it simply swell the agent's pocket? <br /> <br /> And who *physically* protect nodes and ventures Disbursements manage? If Disbursements claims and operates the geothermal harvester built on top of a caern, werewolves, nature spirits and other various supernaturals are going to attempt to &quot;reclaim&quot; and &quot;purify&quot; it in the Wyrd and/or Gaia's name. Syndicate will need very capable security to guard such locations and ensure its secrecy. A special force composed of Extraordinary military, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T11:41:15-07:00","id":1084081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1084047#post1084047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why the Syndicate is collaborating with some elder vampires and occasional Traditionalists without any hesitation or compunction for the sake of so-called &quot;business&quot;? It can be seen as treason from other elements in the Union. Have they no principles or moral compass as members of the Union? What could the Syndicate gain from it? They are toxic partners at the best of times. Is it worth to take risks? And in any case, what business needs Deviant's assistance to flourish? Is Syndicate too incompetent to stand on its own two feet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Expedience. Pragmatism. Cost analysis. Ideological purity is for the proles. Your question only makes sense if the only reason the Union <i>doesn't </i>do something is because it <i>doesn't want to.</i> But the Union has many, many things it simply <i>cannot do </i>or<i>, </i>more pressingly, <i>cannot afford </i>to do.<br /> <br /> When you're Ms. J, the sample Syndicate character, and you have a task that the Union needs done, and the Union does not have the operatives needed to pull it off, the choices are:<br /> 1.) Don't do it, and let whatever bad thing you want to stop happen, <i>even though you could have prevented it.</i><br /> 2.) Pay some Traditionalists to do it, temporarily benefiting a few of your ideological enemies in the short term while achieving your immediate goals with no risk to Union assets.<br /> <br /> What sensible pragmatist would take option 1?<br /> <br /> Knowing when to handle things in-house and when to hire outside contractors is a sign of good business acumen, not weakness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1084047#post1084047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, Disbursement agents have their own occupations and manages their own enterprises, as Posthumanity already pointed out. Then where does operatives' profits go? Who gets them? Agents themselves? Disbursements? Union's annual budget? For instance, if a Disbursement agent runs a food chain, it will yield tones of money and PE. Indeed, IIRC, a Disbursement agent was alluded to own a coffee house chain. Someone have to come and collect it. Or it simply swell the agent's pocket?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who owns it?<br /> <br /> If a Disbursements agent uses their own funds to acquire a business, its profits are theirs. (Imagine how quickly the Syndicate would implode if the Convention thought it could seize the private assets of its members.) If Disbursements is managing a Union front, its profits should be re-invested to keep the front viable and grow its operations, minus some skim for the Union budget and/or a little light embezzlement for the amalgam.<br /> <br /> (A Disbursements-agent-run food chain might not yield PE, no matter how successful it is. Primal Ventures are extraordinary cases, and the only surefire way to create one is Prime 5.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1084047#post1084047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And who *physically* protect nodes and ventures Disbursements manage? If Disbursements claims and operates the geothermal harvester built on top of a caern, werewolves, nature spirits and other various supernaturals are going to attempt to &quot;reclaim&quot; and &quot;purify&quot; it in the Wyrd and/or Gaia's name. Syndicate will need very capable security to guard such locations and ensure its secrecy. A special force composed of Extraordinary military, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Private security, paid for out of the amalgam's budget, likely hired from an Enforcers front. For low-risk, just use well-armed and well-trained Sleepers. For higher-risk, bring in hypertech equipment, Extraordinary mercenaries, and/or Enlightened Enforcers. For extreme high risk, post Iterator combat operatives and constructs to the amalgam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T12:49:23-07:00","id":1084106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1084081#post1084081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Expedience. Pragmatism. Cost analysis. Ideological purity is for the proles. Your question only makes sense if the only reason the Union <i>doesn't </i>do something is because it <i>doesn't want to.</i> But the Union has many, many things it simply <i>cannot do </i>or<i>, </i>more pressingly, <i>cannot afford </i>to do.<br /> <br /> When you're Ms. J, the sample Syndicate character, and you have a task that the Union needs done, and the Union does not have the operatives needed to pull it off, the choices are:<br /> 1.) Don't do it, and let whatever bad thing you want to stop happen, <i>even though you could have prevented it.</i><br /> 2.) Pay some Traditionalists to do it, temporarily benefiting a few of your ideological enemies in the short term while achieving your immediate goals with no risk to Union assets.<br /> <br /> What sensible pragmatist would take option 1?<br /> <br /> Knowing when to handle things in-house and when to hire outside contractors is a sign of good business acumen, not weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditionalists I agree. However, can same logic be applied on collaborating with the <i>vampires</i> for business?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1084081#post1084081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who owns it?<br /> <br /> If a Disbursements agent uses their own funds to acquire a business, its profits are theirs. (Imagine how quickly the Syndicate would implode if the Convention thought it could seize the private assets of its members.) If Disbursements is managing a Union front, its profits should be re-invested to keep the front viable and grow its operations, minus some skim for the Union budget and/or a little light embezzlement for the amalgam.<br /> <br /> (A Disbursements-agent-run food chain might not yield PE, no matter how successful it is. Primal Ventures are extraordinary cases, and the only surefire way to create one is Prime 5.).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no objections whatsoever. Disbursements don't make money - instead it manages, defends, and nurtures Syndicate's Ventures and inspect its growth, as you have already elaborated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1084081#post1084081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Private security, paid for out of the amalgam's budget, likely hired from an Enforcers front. For low-risk, just use well-armed and well-trained Sleepers. For higher-risk, bring in hypertech equipment, Extraordinary mercenaries, and/or Enlightened Enforcers. For extreme high risk, post Iterator combat operatives and constructs to the amalgam.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Now I suppose &quot;node location security&quot; and &quot;our allies&quot; are probably not so different after all.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Enforcer amalgams specialize in eliminating city-dwelling lupines, using recent Progenitor toys to identify them and level the playing field with their own hyper-strength and dermal armor. Beyond that, we don\u2019t hunt down such creatures in their territory; that\u2019s what our allies and fellow Conventions are for. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 04-26-2017, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T18:36:46-07:00","id":1084228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1082756-several-questions-regarding-the-syndicate-and-others?p=1084106#post1084106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionalists I agree. However, can same logic be applied on collaborating with the <i>vampires</i> for business?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure - the same calculations apply. Vampires are pretty good citizens, for RDs. Keep to themselves, mostly feud with one another, have a policy of not causing disturbances in public (most of them, anyway.) Certainly they're not substantially more repugnant than the organized crime types the Syndicate shakes hands with. If uprooting their influence or fighting them is more trouble than it's worth - and it often is, because they're deeply entrenched, insidious, and vindictive - then the smart play is to come to the table and cut a deal.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way: The Union's metaphor for the terrestrial Realm is that it's the <i>Front Lines. </i>There's a war on, and while you and I might not <i>like </i>the regional warlords whose territory is between us and our objective, we don't have the time or the manpower to fight <i>everyone. </i>So we cut a deal and pay for safe passage. This doesn't make us friends, and we're planning on stabbing them in the back - eventually. And they're thinking the same thing. And maybe there's some ideologue back home that thinks that we shouldn't make this sort of compromise, but he's not the one fighting, so if he wants the war fought, he's going to have to suck it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}